Zenify EEVDF/VM latency tuning, rebased for kernel 7.1 (CachyOS base).

Upstream TKG ships this as a vlinux-6.6.1 diff that no longer applies to the
CachyOS 7.1 tree (the base_slice / migration_cost / NR_MIGRATE_BREAK regions
were restructured behind CONFIG_CACHY). Rebased here against the GHOST 7.1
source so the CONFIG_ZENIFY tunables layer cleanly on top of CONFIG_CACHY and
CONFIG_SCHED_GHOST:

  - sched_cfs_bandwidth_slice: ZENIFY 3ms (default 5ms)
  - SCHED_NR_MIGRATE_BREAK: 8 under ZENIFY (already 8 under CACHY)
  - sched_energy_aware: 0 under ZENIFY
  - dirty_background_ratio / vm_dirty_ratio: 20 / 50 under ZENIFY

These hunks share the same layout across the ghost, eevdf and BORE trees, so
this patch is scheduler-independent. sched_migration_cost lives in a region
that BORE restructures, so its ZENIFY override is carried in the per-scheduler
0003-glitched-eevdf-migration-cost.patch / -migration-cost-bore.patch instead.

base_slice is intentionally not touched: CONFIG_CACHY already yields 400us
(== the original ZENIFY value), so no override is needed.

